243
00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:11.450
Well, first, this is something I ask all of my guests.

244
00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.770
Is there a moment in your own life,

245
00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.350
a mishap, a misunderstanding,

246
00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.530
a full-blown meltdown

247
00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.090
that would qualify as a snafu?

248
00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.850
I mean, I have one that immediately comes to mind.

249
00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.090
What is it, lady?

250
00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:31.650
I had just moved from Indonesia to Dallas, Texas in the 80s.

251
00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.490
Okay, 1984.

252
00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.310
I had lived in Jakarta for 12 years.

253
00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:41.850
I didn't know what the heck an American high school vibe was.

254
00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:42.630
Oh, my God.

255
00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:47.090
And I was also a grade ahead in half my subjects.

256
00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.530
So I would go to the junior high for the first four classes.

257
00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:51.910
Then my mom would pick me up.

258
00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.890
I'd eat lunch in the car,

259
00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:55.550
driving to the high school.

260
00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:59.110
And I was like this tiny little thing

261
00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.870
in this big high school.

262
00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.110
I was such an outsider.

263
00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:05.950
And I really wanted to fit in.

264
00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:10.630
And I'm a freshman who's moved from Indonesia,

265
00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.730
who doesn't know, like,

266
00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.050
I'm supposed to get a perm and wear a bunch of eyeliner.

267
00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.270
I don't know that yet.

268
00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.870
